# BP Dumper — canonical Python client

**Canonical product path:** `scripts/bp-dumper-py/` → packaged as `DumperApps.exe`
via `scripts/installer/build-exe.ps1`. Members get auto-detect of the Star Citizen
install (drive search for LIVE / Game.log).

| Client | Status | FS discovery |
|---|---|---|
| Standalone Python / exe | **Canonical** — build + ship this | Drive auto-scan / path prompt OK |
| Store WinUI (`apps/bp-dumper-store/`) | **Parked** — listing may stay live; do not invest in feature parity | FolderPicker only (legacy sandbox experiment) |

Shared wire notes (for webhook / Edge): `scripts/bp-dumper-shared/PROTOCOL.md`.

## When changing BP Dumper

- Prefer changes in **`scripts/bp-dumper-py/`** only.
- Do **not** require Store WinUI updates for new member features.
- Keep `feat(dumper)` / `fix(dumper)` Conventional Commits for semantic-release.

## Do not regress

- Auto-detect / drive search is a **wanted** member feature on the Python/exe client.
- Do not push members back to “pick LIVE folder only” as the primary Windows story
  while the exe path is primary.
